<!-- Determinism — what decides that the two renders produce the same components. Left diagram: one
     SOML tree splits into two branches (the tree the web measured · the tree read back from the PPTX)
     and they meet again at a single equals sign. The branches are `route="elbow"` connectors, so the
     bent lines are recomputed when a box moves. Only the equals circle is `accent3` (green) — on this
     slide green means only "the same".

     On the right, three items unpack what that equals sign actually compares. The check circles use
     the same green, so the diagram and the list read as one sentence. The strip at the bottom is the
     single command that runs all three. -->
<slide id="determinism" enter="rise">
  <text variant="kicker">What decides</text>
  <h1>Both renders, same components</h1>
  <row gap="xl" align="center" grow="1">
    <row gap="0" align="center" w="560">
      <shape type="rounded-rect" id="tree" variant="card" w="130" h="96" pad="sm">
        <col gap="0" justify="center" h="fill"><text role="heading" size="22">SOML</text><text role="caption" size="16">Deck tree</text></col>
      </shape>
      <spacer grow="1"/>
      <col gap="2xl" w="190">
        <shape type="rounded-rect" id="webtree" variant="card" w="fill" h="84" pad="xs sm">
          <col gap="0" justify="center" h="fill"><text role="heading" size="20">Web tree</text><text role="caption" size="16">Chromium · rect</text></col>
        </shape>
        <shape type="rounded-rect" id="pptxtree" variant="card" w="fill" h="84" pad="xs sm">
          <col gap="0" justify="center" h="fill"><text role="heading" size="20">PPTX tree</text><text role="caption" size="16">XML read back</text></col>
        </shape>
      </col>
      <spacer grow="1"/>
      <shape type="ellipse" id="same" fill="accent3" border="none" shadow="soft" w="96" h="96" enter="zoom">
        <text role="title" size="48" color="bg" align="center" anchor="center">=</text>
      </shape>
    </row>
    <col gap="lg" grow="1" basis="0">
      <row gap="md" align="start">
        <shape type="ellipse" fill="accent3" border="none" w="36" h="36"><text role="caption" color="bg" align="center" anchor="center"><strong>✓</strong></text></shape>
        <col gap="0" grow="1" basis="0"><text role="heading" size="24">Parity</text><text role="caption">Same kind · rect · style · order · text runs</text></col>
      </row>
      <row gap="md" align="start">
        <shape type="ellipse" fill="accent3" border="none" w="36" h="36"><text role="caption" color="bg" align="center" anchor="center"><strong>✓</strong></text></shape>
        <col gap="0" grow="1" basis="0"><text role="heading" size="24">Schema</text><text role="caption">Every XML part validates against ECMA-376</text></col>
      </row>
      <row gap="md" align="start">
        <shape type="ellipse" fill="accent3" border="none" w="36" h="36"><text role="caption" color="bg" align="center" anchor="center"><strong>✓</strong></text></shape>
        <col gap="0" grow="1" basis="0"><text role="heading" size="24">Determinism</text><text role="caption">Same input, same bytes</text></col>
      </row>
    </col>
  </row>
  <connector from="tree" to="webtree" route="elbow" from-side="right" to-side="left" enter="draw"/>
  <connector from="tree" to="pptxtree" route="elbow" from-side="right" to-side="left" enter="draw"/>
  <connector from="webtree" to="same" route="elbow" from-side="right" to-side="left" variant="accent" enter="draw"/>
  <connector from="pptxtree" to="same" route="elbow" from-side="right" to-side="left" variant="accent" enter="draw"/>
  <shape type="rounded-rect" fill="surface" border="none" radius="md" w="fill" pad="sm md">
    <row gap="md" align="center" justify="between">
      <text role="code" size="20"><span color="accent3">$</span> go test ./...</text>
      <text role="caption">Where lines wrap is up to each engine — outside the contract.</text>
    </row>
  </shape>
  <note>The only goldens are the layout tree without coordinates and the diagnostics — the parity check re-measures coordinates every run, so a diff only ever says "one more shape".</note>
</slide>
